WEBVTT

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:02.359
Words in context.

00:00:02.359 --> 00:00:04.534
Predict your own word before you look.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:06.596
The passage always hands you a clue.

00:00:08.144 --> 00:00:09.819
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:09.819 --> 00:00:13.269
A blank, or an underlined word, in a short passage.

00:00:13.269 --> 00:00:15.521
And four single words to choose from.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.535
It isn't testing whether you know fancy words.

00:00:19.535 --> 00:00:22.523
It's testing the precise meaning this sentence needs.

00:00:23.581 --> 00:00:24.881
Here's the method.

00:00:24.881 --> 00:00:28.666
First, read the whole passage, not just the sentence with the blank.

00:00:28.666 --> 00:00:29.816
Find the clue.

00:00:29.816 --> 00:00:32.516
Words like but and although flip the meaning.

00:00:32.516 --> 00:00:35.511
A colon, or because, keeps it the same.

00:00:35.511 --> 00:00:39.081
Now predict your own simple word, before you look at the choices.

00:00:39.081 --> 00:00:40.331
Then match it.

00:00:40.331 --> 00:00:44.027
Check the direction, positive or negative, and the strength.

00:00:45.127 --> 00:00:46.627
Four clue rules.

00:00:46.627 --> 00:00:51.922
Contrast clues, like although and but, mean the blank is the opposite of the other idea.

00:00:51.922 --> 00:00:57.922
Restatement clues, like a colon or a dash, mean the blank repeats an idea that's already there.

00:00:57.922 --> 00:00:59.197
Match the tone.

00:00:59.197 --> 00:01:02.522
If the passage is critical, the word can't be a compliment.

00:01:02.522 --> 00:01:05.807
And for underlined words, beware the common meaning.

00:01:05.807 --> 00:01:07.615
Qualified can mean limited.

00:01:08.626 --> 00:01:09.951
Let's try one.

00:01:09.951 --> 00:01:14.376
Although sets up a contrast with her later work, which was remarkably consistent.

00:01:14.376 --> 00:01:17.026
So the blank means the opposite of consistent.

00:01:17.026 --> 00:01:20.676
And right after the blank: results that differed every time.

00:01:20.676 --> 00:01:23.271
So predict a simple word: unreliable.

00:01:23.271 --> 00:01:24.271
Now match.

00:01:24.271 --> 00:01:26.296
Influential is positive.

00:01:26.296 --> 00:01:28.521
Inexpensive is about cost.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.446
Meticulous means careful.

00:01:30.446 --> 00:01:32.946
Inconsistent matches unreliable.

00:01:32.946 --> 00:01:34.225
The answer is A.

00:01:35.306 --> 00:01:37.356
Watch out for the topic word.

00:01:37.356 --> 00:01:43.996
It sounds related to science, or art, or whatever the passage is about, but it doesn't fit the logic.

00:01:43.996 --> 00:01:46.330
Match your prediction, not the topic.

00:01:47.377 --> 00:01:49.262
Here's the lesson on one page.

00:01:49.262 --> 00:01:50.317
How to spot it.

00:01:50.317 --> 00:01:51.767
The four steps.

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:53.147
The clue rules.

00:01:53.147 --> 00:01:54.172
And the trap.

00:01:54.172 --> 00:01:56.941
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
